# internal_coordinates

Molecular-structure analysis: retain bonds and formal charges from MOL/SDF; infer bonds once for coordinate-only inputs (xyz/pdb/cif). Analyze stereochemistry, rings, and rotatable dihedrals; detect anomalous bond lengths (compressed/elongated/breaking_suspect/forming/atomic overlap) and anomalous angles; and write a Z-matrix internal-coordinate file along a spanning tree of the molecular graph. Can also convert a Z-matrix back to Cartesian. mode=transform applies rigid internal-coordinate edits to the Cartesian coordinates — rotate a group about an axis/bond, stretch or compress a bond by translating one fragment, invert a chiral center by swapping two branches — or edits the covalent topology by replacing a substituent with a new group given as SMILES, then re-validates the edited geometry (bond/angle anomaly detection) and returns the transformed xyz. Set output_path to .mol/.sdf to save the edited molecule with its bonds and formal charges. Gives the model accurate structural facts without looking at a picture. REQUIRED before ts_guess scan_prepare/interpolate or any TS/scan work: scan/watch atom indices and reaction coordinates must come from this analyze report (forming/breaking bonds, dihedrals, clashes) — never from guessing XYZ indices or reading a picture. Also required to verify dihedral/angle preorganization that distance_filters cannot express. Use for: TS inspection (locating breaking/forming bonds), conformational analysis, stereo confirmation, geometry sanity checks, Z-matrix edits. Do not use for: plain format conversion (use format_converter) or generating a structure from SMILES (use smiles_to_mol).

## Input and result contract

```typescript
interface ToolResponse<T> {
  call_id: string;
  is_success: boolean;
  summary: string;
  data: T;
  duration_ms: number;
}

type InternalCoordinatesArgs = {
  /** analyze: structure-perception analysis and write a Z-matrix file (default); zmatrix_to_cartesian: restore Cartesian coordinates from Z-matrix text/file; transform: apply rigid internal-coordinate operations (see 'operations') to the Cartesian coordinates, validate the edited geometry, and return the transformed xyz. (default="analyze") */
  "mode"?: "analyze" | "zmatrix_to_cartesian" | "transform";
  /** Input file path (xyz/mol/pdb/sdf/cif or one Gaussian Cartesian input in Angstrom/Bohr). MOL/SDF retain their bonds and formal charges. Used when mode=analyze or transform. (default=null) */
  "input_path"?: string | null;
  /** Structure text in input_format. If input_path is set, the file is read instead. (default=null) */
  "input_text"?: string | null;
  /** Input format. auto uses the file extension, or recognizes MOL/SDF text; Gaussian Cartesian input is recognized from content for files or text; other coordinate text must be valid XYZ. (default="auto") */
  "input_format"?: "auto" | "xyz" | "mol" | "pdb" | "sdf" | "cif";
  /** Total charge for coordinate-only input. Omit to inherit a Gaussian declaration, otherwise default 0. An explicit value must match Gaussian charge. MOL/SDF use their stored formal charges. (default=0) */
  "charge"?: number;
  /** Optional reaction-center atom indices (1-based). When set, the report includes bonded-neighbor distances and key angles for these atoms. (default=null) */
  "reactive_atoms"?: Array<number> | null;
  /** Optional atom pairs to monitor explicitly (1-based). The report gives distances and a bonded/forming (distance heuristic)/undecidable/far verdict; crowded H...H contacts are never reported as forming. (default=null) */
  "watch_pairs"?: Array<Array<number>> | null;
  /** Bond-length deviation threshold as a fraction. measured/reference ≤ 1-threshold → compressed; ≥ 1+threshold → elongated (≥1.5 → breaking_suspect). (default=0.15) */
  "bond_tolerance"?: number;
  /** Bond-angle deviation threshold (degrees). Reported only when the deviation from the hybridization-expected angle exceeds this. Default 12°. (default=12.0) */
  "angle_tolerance"?: number;
  /** Z-matrix output path when mode=analyze. Default: <stem>.zmat next to input_path; ./structure.zmat for text-only input. (default=null) */
  "zmat_path"?: string | null;
  /** Z-matrix file path when mode=zmatrix_to_cartesian (preferred over zmatrix_text). (default=null) */
  "zmatrix_path"?: string | null;
  /** Z-matrix text when mode=zmatrix_to_cartesian. (default=null) */
  "zmatrix_text"?: string | null;
  /** Output path: transform writes MOL/SDF for .mol/.sdf, preserving the molecular graph; otherwise XYZ. zmatrix_to_cartesian writes XYZ. (default=null) */
  "output_path"?: string | null;
  /** Transform operations, required when mode=transform (rejected in other modes). Applied in order on a copy of the coordinates; all atom indices are 1-based, matching the analyze report; fragment selection uses the input MOL/SDF bonds, or connectivity perceived once for coordinate-only input. Four operation types: (1) rotate — 'axis_atoms': [i, j] defines the rotation axis, 'degrees': angle in degrees, plus exactly one group selector: 'atoms': [...] (explicit 1-based atom list) or 'side_of_bond': [a, b] (rotate the fragment on the b side of bond a-b; fails when a-b is on a ring). Example: {"type": "rotate", "axis_atoms": [3, 7], "side_of_bond": [3, 7], "degrees": 120}. (2) stretch — 'atoms': [i, j] (must be a bonded pair), plus exactly one of 'delta': d (relative change) or 'new_length': L (absolute target), both in Angstrom; the fragment on the j side of bond i-j is translated along the i->j direction. Example: {"type": "stretch", "atoms": [3, 7], "new_length": 2.10}. (3) invert_chirality — 'center': c, 'swap': [n1, n2] (n1/n2 must both be bonded neighbors of c); the two branches are rigidly swapped, inverting the stereocenter. Example: {"type": "invert_chirality", "center": 5, "swap": [6, 9]}. (4) replace_group — topology edit: 'bond': [a, b] (1-based bonded pair, not on a ring) cuts bond a-b, removes the whole fragment on the b side, and attaches a new substituent to atom a; 'smiles': the new group with exactly one [*] dummy atom marking the attachment point (e.g. '[*]C(=O)O' for -COOH, '[*]c1ccccc1' for phenyl, '[*]F' for -F). The substituent's 3D geometry is embedded and force-field optimized, then docked along the old a->b direction at the reference bond length; the new bond order comes from the [*] bond in the SMILES (default single). Surviving atoms keep their order and the new atoms are appended; operations listed after a replace_group use the NEW atom numbering. Example: {"type": "replace_group", "bond": [3, 7], "smiles": "[*]C(=O)O"}. (default=null) */
  "operations"?: Array<{
  [key: string]: unknown;
}> | null;
};

type InternalCoordinatesData = {
  /** Whether the operation succeeded */
  "is_success": boolean;
  /** Structured analysis report when mode=analyze (sectioned text) (default="") */
  "report"?: string;
  /** Machine-readable list of bond/angle anomalies; each item has type/atoms/value/reference/status. When mode=transform, these are measured on the transformed coordinates. */
  "anomalies"?: Array<{
  [key: string]: unknown;
}>;
  /** Per-operation summaries when mode=transform: type, target atoms, parameters, and the 1-based list/count of atoms moved */
  "operations_applied"?: Array<{
  [key: string]: unknown;
}>;
  /** Bond/angle anomalies of the input structure before the transform (mode=transform) */
  "anomalies_before"?: Array<{
  [key: string]: unknown;
}>;
  /** Z-matrix file path written when mode=analyze (default="") */
  "zmat_path"?: string;
  /** Line count of the Z-matrix file when mode=analyze (default=0) */
  "zmat_lines"?: number;
  /** Z-matrix export status, reported separately from the geometry analysis: 'written' = file produced; 'failed' = export failed while the analysis succeeded (see zmat_error); 'not_requested' = other mode. (default="not_requested") */
  "zmat_status"?: "written" | "failed" | "not_requested";
  /** Why the Z-matrix export failed (only set when zmat_status='failed'). A failed export never hides the completed distance/angle measurements. (default="") */
  "zmat_error"?: string;
  /** xyz text returned when mode=zmatrix_to_cartesian or transform (default="") */
  "xyz_text"?: string;
  /** File path written when mode=zmatrix_to_cartesian or transform (default="") */
  "output_path"?: string;
  /** Status or error message (default="") */
  "message"?: string;
};

declare const tools: {
  /** Molecular-structure analysis: retain bonds and formal charges from MOL/SDF; infer bonds once for coordinate-only inputs (xyz/pdb/cif). Analyze stereochemistry, rings, and rotatable dihedrals; detect anomalous bond lengths (compressed/elongated/breaking_suspect/forming/atomic overlap) and anomalous angles; and write a Z-matrix internal-coordinate file along a spanning tree of the molecular graph. Can also convert a Z-matrix back to Cartesian. mode=transform applies rigid internal-coordinate edits to the Cartesian coordinates — rotate a group about an axis/bond, stretch or compress a bond by translating one fragment, invert a chiral center by swapping two branches — or edits the covalent topology by replacing a substituent with a new group given as SMILES, then re-validates the edited geometry (bond/angle anomaly detection) and returns the transformed xyz. Set output_path to .mol/.sdf to save the edited molecule with its bonds and formal charges. Gives the model accurate structural facts without looking at a picture. REQUIRED before ts_guess scan_prepare/interpolate or any TS/scan work: scan/watch atom indices and reaction coordinates must come from this analyze report (forming/breaking bonds, dihedrals, clashes) — never from guessing XYZ indices or reading a picture. Also required to verify dihedral/angle preorganization that distance_filters cannot express. Use for: TS inspection (locating breaking/forming bonds), conformational analysis, stereo confirmation, geometry sanity checks, Z-matrix edits. Do not use for: plain format conversion (use format_converter) or generating a structure from SMILES (use smiles_to_mol). */
  internal_coordinates(args: InternalCoordinatesArgs): Promise<ToolResponse<InternalCoordinatesData>>;
};

declare function text(value: unknown): void;
```

## Calling pattern

Construct args from the contract and the actual task declarations. This pattern does not supply scientific methods or other task inputs.

```javascript
const r = await tools.internal_coordinates(args);
if (r.is_success) text(r.data); else text(r.summary);
```

